thought this line of reasoning was specious the first time I heard it, but
apparently it's been statistically verified that seat belt laws have had
this sort of effect (source: "Environmental Pseudoscience," a talk given
by Leon Llouw at an ISIL conference).

He speculates that something that made driving seem riskier to the driver
would make them drive more safely, like a big spearhead sticking out at
the chest from the steering wheel.

