From: rjc@gnu.ai.mit.edu (Ray)
Date: Thu, 27 Jan 94 9:09:14 WET
Subject: [#94-1-582] META: go moderate yourself

   The problem with your proposal is that it simply will not work
in practice. Ok, you exclude foo. What happens next? bar quotes
a message by foo and responds to it. Now you have to exclude bar
also if you still want to prevent seeing foo's messages. But baz,
zab, snazzle, and fuzzle are also now joined in the flame discussion
so they must be excluded also. exclude works when there's no flame war,
it won't when everybody is responding to one disruptor. 

   The purpose of moderation isn't to simply stop the posts of that one
person, it's to stop the chain reaction caused by that person. I mean,
if the people on this list are so anti-authority that they can't even
respond to the requests of a ``party host'' to maintain courtesy without
equating it to an Orwellian government conspiracy, then maybe they
should refrain from libertarian politics and lobby for the right to do 
anything on anyone else's property.

   If people really want this list to be a free for all, fine. Myself,
I'll just exclude all, and include like three or four people and be
done with it.

   Frankly, I'm sick to death of debating the whole thing. It seems
to be a _stupid_ thing to be arguing about. It's so trivial. A list
administrator telling you to calm down or shut up isn't the end of the
world.

